# Colmeia - Dados e Dominio

## Escopo

Este arquivo registra convencoes especificas do repositorio sobre dominio e
fluxo de dados.

## Estrategia de Dados

- Use REST for authentication, session bootstrap and hub resource management.
- Agent queries use REST or Socket/relay through the existing transport
  abstraction and configured fallback policy. Socket carries query results
  as well as presence and invalidation events.
- Keep transport selection, retry, cancellation and concurrency policies out
  of UI and domain repositories. Reuse the existing gates and coalescers.
- Do not retry authorization failures or cancelled work through another
  transport. Preserve deadlines across fallback and avoid duplicate dispatch.
- Local-only reads must not attempt REST or Socket. Agent unavailability is
  not evidence that the browser itself has no internet connection.

## Hub Plug (plug_server) — documentacao de apoio no repo

A especificacao normativa do bridge vive no repositorio **plug_server** (e schemas
no **plug_agente**). No Colmeia, use estes resumos para nao depender só da memoria:

- `docs/plug_server_docs_index_for_colmeia.md` — mapa da pasta `docs` do hub
  (REST vs Socket, relay, Client/Agent, limites, escala)
- `docs/bridge_agent_sql_api_options.md` — `sql.execute`: `multi_result`,
  `sql.executeBatch`, batch JSON-RPC, paginacao, `execution_mode`

## Cache Local

- Keep opportunistic caches bounded and separate from user-selected offline
  packages. Product limits belong to `project_product_scope.mdc`.
- Expose cache access through `AppCacheStore` rather than leaking `Hive`,
  `Box` or IndexedDB transactions to features.
- Use chaves logicas, TTL por recurso e invalidacao explicita
- Sempre permita refresh manual para dados que possam ficar desatualizados
- Offline packages reuse current queries and use cases; do not add full-table
  downloads or new SQL solely to populate them.
- Scope datasets by user, authorized store/agent, query parameters, format
  version and period. Record collection time, completeness and partial days.
- Publish a temporary generation only after completion and permission
  revalidation. Failure, cancellation or quota exhaustion preserves the
  previous generation; do not silently evict selected packages.
- Keep derived snapshots and open periods separate from consolidated facts.
- Coordinate downloads across tabs and reuse existing concurrency limits.
  Resume overdue work on reconnection or foreground entry using the configured
  schedule interval (two hours by default), after validating permissions;
  support manual refresh and preserve explicitly configured intervals.
- Missing datasets or unsupported filter combinations require connection;
  they are not empty results. Offline filtering and export use available data.

## Autenticacao e Autorizacao

- O backend e a fonte final de verdade para autenticacao e autorizacao
- O app pode ocultar telas, menus, botoes, dashboards e relatorios nao
  permitidos, mas nao deve atuar como autoridade final de acesso
- Consultas sensiveis devem considerar usuario autenticado, lojas permitidas,
  recursos concedidos e filtros autorizados
- Modele permissoes por usuario, perfil, escopo de loja e recursos habilitados,
  nao por um cargo estatico unico
- Offline authorization is server-issued, user-bound and scoped to permitted
  stores/agents. Enforce its absolute expiry on reads; local refreshes cannot
  extend it. An expired access token cannot authenticate remote calls.
- Transient network failures must not erase persisted sessions. Confirmed
  revocation removes the affected data and cancels pending work.
- Logout immediately blocks local access, cancels synchronization, removes
  private user data and propagates the change to other tabs.

## Dashboards Dinamicos

- Prefira contratos de backend que retornem metadados suficientes para ajustar
  dashboards sem publicar nova versao a cada pequena mudanca
- Widgets dinamicos devem carregar identificador, tipo, titulo, fonte de dados,
  parametros, ordem e regras de exibicao
- Para graficos interativos, prefira contratos que descrevam series, eixos,
  tooltips, intervalos e comportamento de interacao
- Evite telas bespoke por relatorio ou dashboard quando um renderer
  configuravel for suficiente

## Relatorios Parametrizados

- Prefira metadados fornecidos pelo backend para parametros de relatorio sempre
  que possivel
- Cada parametro deve descrever tipo, obrigatoriedade, valor inicial, opcoes
  permitidas e regras de exibicao
- Prefer server-side filtering, sorting and pagination for online queries;
  prepared offline datasets follow the local-read policy above
- Use formularios dinamicos na UI para que regras especificas de relatorio nao
  sejam duplicadas
- Quando um parametro precisar de formatacao brasileira recorrente, prefira
  helpers centralizados construidos sobre `brasil_fields`

## Value Objects

- Use value objects para entradas com regras proprias, como email, documento,
  periodos, identificadores e filtros estruturados
- Prefira schemas pequenos com `zard` para validar value objects
- Value objects devem expor valores normalizados e manter igualdade por valor
- Nao espalhe regex e validacao de string entre UI, controller e mapper ao
  mesmo tempo

